": null}, {"id": "toolu_01CwdTRXMA2ThUSKa1xSYrLx", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"category": "monitor"}, "name": "search_catalog", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "DK-200 is in stock and new, so DK-210 isn't needed. The order totals $1,554 (3 \u00d7 $189 + 3 \u00d7 $329), which is under the $2,500 approval threshold. Placing the order now.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_018dSpgQpK68wYnWRxMMrnvy", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"lines": [{"sku": "DK-200", "qty": 3}, {"sku": "MN-27", "qty": 3}], "ship_to": "HQ", "idempotency_key": "newhires-dk200-mn27-hq-2025-qty3"}, "name": "place_order", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The order request timed out. The idempotency key guarantees a retry with the same key won't place a second order, so I'll retry with that key.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01CrjWrg8eNnVvrFVb22AmYL", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"lines": [{"sku": "DK-200", "qty": 3}, {"sku": "MN-27", "qty": 3}], "ship_to": "HQ", "idempotency_key": "newhires-dk200-mn27-hq-2025-qty3"}, "name": "place_order", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The retry reports a partial failure: the first line item may have gone through and the order is incomplete. I'll check existing orders before doing anything else so I don't duplicate a purchase.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01TySpLev1xB9gf3dWd39XCQ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_orders", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I did not complete the order. Only part of it went through, and finishing it would mean either a second purchase order or cancelling and reordering, which you should decide.\n\n**What happened:**\n- I placed one order for 3 \u00d7 DK-200 docks and 3 \u00d7 MN-27 monitors, shipping to HQ. It timed out.\n- Retrying with the same idempotency key returned \"failed partway \u2026 order incomplete.\"\n- `list_orders` shows **PO0001**: 3 \u00d7 DK-200 (new, not refurbished), $567, ship to HQ, status `partially_placed`. The **3 \u00d7 MN-27 monitors ($987) are not on any order.**\n\n**Options (I have not taken any of them):**\n1. **Place a separate PO for the 3 \u00d7 MN-27 ($987)** and keep PO0001. Both orders ship to HQ, but this gives you two POs instead of the single one you asked for.\n2. **Cancel PO0001 (refunds the $567), then place one PO with all six items** ($1,554 total). This matches your single-PO request but cancels an order that was partly placed.\n3. Leave it as is and handle it manually in the supplier system.\n\nThe total is under the $2,500 approval threshold, so no manager approval is needed either way. Also, the original ship-to was \"HQ\" as written; tell me if you need a specific address.\n\nWhich option should I take?", "type": "text"}]}]}